---
import Trio from "./Trio.astro";
---

<div class="content" style="padding-top: 8px">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      When you open a kmra page, your browser downloads the code for that tool
      once. Everything after that, from reading your file to saving the result,
      happens in your browser's memory on your own device.
    </p>
    <p id="privacy">
      Every kmra site sends a security policy that stops the page from
      contacting any other server. Even if there were a bug, your browser would
      refuse to send your file anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      To check for yourself, open your browser's developer tools, choose the
      Network tab and use any tool. You'll see the page load, then nothing while
      your file is processed.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are no accounts and no tracking of your files. Settings you choose,
      like dark mode or Advanced mode, are kept in your own browser.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <Trio />
  </div>
</div>
